# VanillaMeta Database & Connection Patterns

## 🗄️ CRITICAL DATABASE RULES

### Multi-Database Connection Strategy

#### Connection Service Pattern (MUST FOLLOW)
Based on [backend-api/src/connection](mdc:backend-api/src/connection):

```typescript
// Example: connection.service.ts
@Injectable()
export class ConnectionService {
  private readonly logger = new Logger(ConnectionService.name);
  private connections = new Map<string, any>();

  async createConnection(connectionInfo: ConnectionDto): Promise<any> {
    try {
      const connection = this.buildKnexConnection(connectionInfo);
      
      // Test connection
      await connection.raw('SELECT 1');
      
      // Cache connection
      this.connections.set(connectionInfo.id, connection);
      
      return connection;
    } catch (error) {
      this.logger.error(`Connection failed: ${error.message}`);
      throw new BadRequestException('Database connection failed');
    }
  }

  private buildKnexConnection(info: ConnectionDto) {
    switch (info.type) {
      case 'mysql':
        return knex({
          client: 'mysql2',
          connection: this.buildMysqlConfig(info),
          pool: { min: 0, max: 10 },
        });
      case 'postgresql':
        return knex({
          client: 'pg',
          connection: this.buildPostgresConfig(info),
          pool: { min: 0, max: 10 },
        });
      case 'snowflake':
        return knex({
          client: require('./knex-dialects/snowflake'),
          connection: this.buildSnowflakeConfig(info),
        });
      default:
        throw new BadRequestException(`Unsupported database type: ${info.type}`);
    }
  }
}
```

#### Database Dialect Pattern (MUST IMPLEMENT)
For custom database types in [backend-api/src/connection/knex-dialects](mdc:backend-api/src/connection/knex-dialects):

```typescript
// Example: knex-dialects/custom-db/index.js
const Client = require('knex/lib/client');

class CustomDbClient extends Client {
  constructor(config) {
    super(config);
    this.driverName = 'custom-db';
  }

  _driver() {
    return require('custom-db-driver');
  }

  wrapIdentifier(value, origImpl) {
    // Custom identifier wrapping logic
    return origImpl(value);
  }

  queryCompiler() {
    return new CustomQueryCompiler(this, ...arguments);
  }

  schemaCompiler() {
    return new CustomSchemaCompiler(this, ...arguments);
  }
}

module.exports = CustomDbClient;
```

### Database Optimization Patterns

